1          /* SAS program to accompany the article
2             "On reducing the spread of coronavirus"
                                                           The SAS System

3             by Rick Wicklin, published 08Apr2020 on The DO Loop blog:
4             https://blogs.sas.com/content/iml/2020/04/08/reducing-spread-of-coronavirus.html
5          
6             This program shows that the public-health mandates to reduce the spread of the
7             coronovirus (COVID-19) are supported by a very simple mathematical
8             model, the cumulative geometric distribution. The cumulative distribution
9             shows the probability that an event occurs on the n_th trial when the
10            probability in each trial is the same value, p.
11         
12            The public health mandates do two things:
13            1. Reduce the number of interactions: stay at home, social distancing, prohibit congregating,...
14            2. Reduce the probability that an interaction results in a new infection: wash hands,
15               sanitize surfaces, wear a mask,....
16            In addition, the model shows that even if the probability of an infdection is low, it can
17            still happen in only a few interactions. Lastly, the model quantifies the how the
18            cumulative probability increase as a function of the number of trials when p << 1.
19         */
20         
21         /* COVID=19 application */
22         data Geometric;
23         do p = 0.0001, 0.001, 0.01;
24            do n = 0 to 180;    /* event occurs on the n_th trial */
25               /* there are n-1 trials for which the event did NOT occur */
26               pdf = pdf("Geometric", n-1, p);  /* number of trials before first event */
27               cdf = cdf("Geometric", n-1, p);  /* probability that event happens on or before n_th Trial*/
28               cdf2 = 1 - (1-p)**n;    /* explicit formula */
29               cdfApprox = n*p;
30               output;
31            end;
32         end;
33         run;

